ortugal and Spain shared the same monarch, and by establishing the House of Braganza on the Portuguese throne.\nBefore becoming king, he was John II, the 8th Duke of Braganza. He was the grandson of Catherine, Duchess of Braganza, a claimant to the crown during the Portuguese succession crisis of 1580. On the eve of his death in 1656, the Portuguese Empire was at its territorial zenith, spanning the globe.","wp_description":"King of Portugal from 1640 to 1656","wikipedia_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_IV_of_Portugal","image_lead":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e0/Portrait_of_John%2C_Duke_of_Braganza_c._1630_%28The_Royal_Castle_in_Warsaw%29.png","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Portrait_of_John%2C_Duke_of_Braganza_c._1630_%28The_Royal_Castle_in_Warsaw%29.png/960px-Portrait_of_John%2C_Duke_of_Braganza_c._1630_%28The_Royal_Castle_in_Warsaw%29.png","chat_ready":true,"display_from":1640,"display_to":1656}